{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "recall-radar",
    "summary": "A unified US product-recalls API: FDA, CPSC, and NHTSA in one searchable JSON feed.",
    "description": "\nOne API for every US product recall.\n\nThe US government publishes recalls across several unrelated agencies, in\ndifferent shapes, with different quirks. **recall-radar** fetches them daily,\nnormalizes them into a single schema, and serves them as clean, searchable JSON.\n\n### Coverage\n\n| Agency | Covers | Records |\n|---|---|---|\n| **FDA** | Food, drug, and device recalls | 86,683 |\n| **NHTSA** | Vehicles, tires, child seats | 15,138 |\n| **CPSC** | Consumer products | 9,912 |\n\nCurrently **3 agencies, 111,733 recalls**, going back to 1973 for CPSC.\nUSDA FSIS (meat and poultry) is not yet included — its upstream API is\nunreachable behind bot protection.\n\n### Response shape\n\nEvery successful list response is `{data, pagination, meta}`; single-item\nresponses are `{data, meta}`. Every error is `{\"error\": {code, message, detail}}`.\n\n### Refresh cadence\n\nFDA data refreshes roughly weekly upstream; NHTSA and CPSC daily. Ingestion\nruns every day at 06:00 UTC, so a day with no new FDA rows is normal.\n\n### Authentication\n\nRequests must carry the `X-RapidAPI-Proxy-Secret` header, which RapidAPI adds\nautomatically. `/health` is always open.\n",
    "contact": {
      "name": "recall-radar",
      "url": "https://github.com/sm-coding-projects/recall-radar"
    },
    "license": {
      "name": "Source data: US Government public domain"
    },
    "version": "0.1.0"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://recall-radar.onrender.com",
      "description": "Production"
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/health": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "meta"
        ],
        "summary": "Service health",
        "description": "Liveness check, including a real database round-trip.\n\n**This endpoint never requires authentication**, so it can be used as an\nuptime check without exposing your proxy secret.\n\nReturns `200` even when the database is unreachable — with\n`\"status\": \"degraded\"` and `\"database\": \"unavailable\"` — so that a briefly\nsuspended database does not flap an external health check. Use the\n`status` field, not the HTTP code, to distinguish the two.\n\nThe `recalls` field is the total row count, and is `null` when degraded.",
        "operationId": "getHealth",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Service and database are both healthy.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Health"
                },
                "example": {
                  "status": "ok",
                  "database": "ok",
                  "recalls": 111733,
                  "version": "0.1.0"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/recalls": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "recalls"
        ],
        "summary": "List recalls with filters and pagination",
        "description": "Browse recalls across all agencies, newest first.\n\nResults are ordered by `recall_date` descending. All filters are optional\nand combine with AND.\n\n- `agency` — exact match, case-insensitive (`FDA`, `CPSC`, `NHTSA`)\n- `category` — case-insensitive **substring** match, so `category=food`\n  matches `Food`, and `category=brake` matches NHTSA component names\n- `since` / `until` — inclusive bounds on `recall_date` (`YYYY-MM-DD`)\n\nPagination caps at **100 per page**; asking for more returns `422`.\n`pagination.total` is the count of all matches, not just this page, so you\ncan size a full pull before making it.\n\nPassing a `since` later than `until` returns `400` rather than an empty\npage, so a swapped-argument bug surfaces instead of looking like no data.\n\nEvery parameter may be sent blank (`?agency=&since=`) — a blank value means\n\"not supplied\", which is what API gateways emit for unset optional fields.",
        "operationId": "listRecalls",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "agency",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "Filter by agency, case-insensitive. Blank means no filter.",
              "examples": [
                "CPSC"
              ],
              "title": "Agency"
            },
            "description": "Filter by agency, case-insensitive. Blank means no filter."
          },
          {
            "name": "category",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "Case-insensitive substring match on category. Blank means no filter.",
              "examples": [
                "Food"
              ],
              "title": "Category"
            },
            "description": "Case-insensitive substring match on category. Blank means no filter."
          },
          {
            "name": "since",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "date"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "Only recalls on or after this date. Blank means no lower bound.",
              "examples": [
                "2026-07-01"
              ],
              "title": "Since"
            },
            "description": "Only recalls on or after this date. Blank means no lower bound."
          },
          {
            "name": "until",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "date"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "Only recalls on or before this date. Blank means no upper bound.",
              "examples": [
                "2026-07-31"
              ],
              "title": "Until"
            },
            "description": "Only recalls on or before this date. Blank means no upper bound."
          },
          {
            "name": "page",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 1
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "1-based page number. Blank defaults to 1.",
              "examples": [
                1
              ],
              "title": "Page"
            },
            "description": "1-based page number. Blank defaults to 1."
          },
          {
            "name": "per_page",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "maximum": 100,
                  "minimum": 1
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "Results per page, max 100. Blank defaults to 25.",
              "examples": [
                25
              ],
              "title": "Per Page"
            },
            "description": "Results per page, max 100. Blank defaults to 25."
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "A page of matching recalls.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ListResponse_Recall_"
                },
                "example": {
                  "data": [
                    {
                      "id": 401,
                      "agency": "CPSC",
                      "source_id": "26636",
                      "product": "Sviyatp Pool Drain Covers",
                      "hazard": "The recalled drain covers violate the entrapment protection standards of the Virginia Graeme Baker Pool and Spa Safety Act (VGBA), posing deadly entrapment and drowning hazards to consumers.",
                      "classification": "Refund",
                      "recall_date": "2026-07-23",
                      "published_at": "2026-07-24T00:00:00Z",
                      "url": "https://www.cpsc.gov/Recalls/2026/Sviyatp-Pool-Drain-Covers-Recalled-Due-to-Risk-of-Serious-Injury-or-Death-from-Entrapment-and-Drowning-Hazards",
                      "ingested_at": "2026-07-31T04:07:22.046254Z"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": 513,
                      "agency": "NHTSA",
                      "source_id": "26V481000",
                      "product": "AMG GLB35 4MATIC; C 300; C 300 4MATIC; CLE 300 4MATIC (+24 more) (2019-2026)",
                      "brand": "MERCEDES-BENZ",
                      "category": "LATCHES/LOCKS/LINKAGES:DOORS:LOCK",
                      "hazard": "The micro-switch in the driver's door lock may corrode and fail to detect an open door, preventing the electronic parking brake from engaging automatically. This may result in a vehicle rollaway.",
                      "classification": "Vehicle",
                      "recall_date": "2026-07-24",
                      "published_at": "2026-07-27T00:00:00Z",
                      "url": "https://www.nhtsa.gov/recalls?nhtsaId=26V481000",
                      "ingested_at": "2026-07-31T04:07:31.164779Z"
                    }
                  ],
                  "pagination": {
                    "page": 1,
                    "per_page": 25,
                    "total": 9912,
                    "total_pages": 397,
                    "has_next": true,
                    "has_prev": false
                  },
                  "meta": {
                    "filters": {
                      "agency": "CPSC",
                      "since": "2026-07-01"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "The parameters parsed correctly but do not make sense together.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "error": {
                    "code": "bad_request",
                    "message": "`since` must not be after `until`."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "A parameter failed validation, e.g. per_page above 100 or a malformed date.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "error": {
                    "code": "invalid_parameters",
                    "message": "One or more query parameters are invalid.",
                    "detail": [
                      {
                        "field": "per_page",
                        "reason": "Input should be less than or equal to 100"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "The request did not come through RapidAPI.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "error": {
                    "code": "unauthorized",
                    "message": "Missing or invalid X-RapidAPI-Proxy-Secret header."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Unexpected server error. Details are logged server-side, never returned.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "error": {
                    "code": "internal_error",
                    "message": "An unexpected error occurred."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/recalls/latest": {
